Backport 1/1 commits from #107099.

/cc @cockroachdb/release

---

Fixes #106260

Previously `CREATE TABLE AS`/`CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW AS` sourcing from `SHOW <show_subcmd> <table>` generated a failing schema change job with a `relation "tbl" does not exist error` because the SHOW source table was not fully qualified.

This PR fixes this by respecting the `Builder.qualifyDataSourceNamesInAST` flag in `delegate.TryDelegate()` which implements the failing SHOW commands.

Release note (bug fix): Fix failing schema change job when CREATE TABLE AS or CREATE MATERAILIZED VIEW AS sources from a SHOW command:
1. CREATE TABLE t AS SELECT * FROM [SHOW CREATE TABLE tbl];
2. CREATE TABLE t AS SELECT * FROM [SHOW INDEXES FROM tbl];
3. CREATE TABLE t AS SELECT * FROM [SHOW COLUMNS FROM tbl];
4. CREATE TABLE t AS SELECT * FROM [SHOW CONSTRAINTS FROM tbl];
5. CREATE TABLE t AS SELECT * FROM [SHOW PARTITIONS FROM TABLE tbl];
6. CREATE TABLE t AS SELECT * FROM [SHOW PARTITIONS FROM INDEX tbl@tbl_pkey];

Release justification: Fix broken CTAS/CMVAS statements.

## Description
 The [Table Question Answering](https://huggingface.co/docs/api-inference/detailed_parameters#table-question-answering-task) is one of the Natural Language Processing tasks supported by Hugging Face.

VulcanSQL supports the Using **Table Question Answering** by using the `huggingface_table_question_answering` filter.

```sql
{% set data = [
  {
    "repository": "vulcan-sql",
    "topic": ["analytics", "data-lake", "data-warehouse", "api-builder"],
    "description":"Create and share Data APIs fast! Data API framework for DuckDB, ClickHouse, Snowflake, BigQuery, PostgreSQL"
  },
  {
    "repository": "accio",
    "topic": ["data-analytics", "data-lake", "data-warehouse", "bussiness-intelligence"],
    "description": "Query Your Data Warehouse Like Exploring One Big View."
  },
  {
    "repository": "hell-word",
    "topic": [],
    "description": "Sample repository for testing"
  }
] %}

-- The source data from "huggingface_table_question_answering" need array of object type.
SELECT {{ data | huggingface_table_question_answering(query="How many repositories related to data-lake topic?") }}
```

Sample 2:

```sql
{% req products %}
  SELECT * FROM products
{% endreq %}


SELECT {{ products.value() | huggingface_table_question_answering(query="How many products related to 3C type?", model="microsoft/tapex-base-finetuned-wtq", wait_for_model=true, use_cache=true) }}
```

For more information, please see [README](https://github.com/Canner/vulcan-sql/blob/feature/huggingface-table-question-answering/packages/extension-huggingface/README.md)


## Screenshot
![截圖 2023-07-21 下午12 35 50](https://github.com/Canner/vulcan-sql/assets/5389253/a085a0b2-5cbd-4736-8ed7-eb1cd117526a)
![截圖 2023-07-21 下午12 37 01](https://github.com/Canner/vulcan-sql/assets/5389253/c86a96e9-5f83-4b13-b272-6ee447e81f87)


## Additional Context
- After discussing with @cyyeh, wrote the Hugging Face Filter [Document](https://github.com/Canner/vulcan-sql/blob/feature/huggingface-table-question-answering/packages/doc/docs/extensions/huggingface-table-question-answering.mdx) and put it under extensions temporarily, because the current official website does not provide a location to describe extensions, it may need to discussion to complete the official website for displaying more detailed functions, e.g: dbt extension
- Originally, we use `huggingface.js` library to handle `tableQuestionAnswering` task, but it needed Node.js 18+, so we remove the library and change to send API by `axios`
- Add a timeout for some Jest test cases in other packages that often fail because they exceed the timeout when running test cases in circles. 
- ⚠️ **Caution**: Hugging Face has a [rate limit](https://huggingface.co/docs/api-inference/faq#rate-limits), so it does not allow sending large datasets to the Hugging Face library for processing. Otherwise, using a different Hugging Face model may yield different results or even result in failure.

